title: Announcing Appwrite 2.6 for self-hosted deployments
date: 2026-10-21
cover: /images/changelog/2026-10-21.avif
tags: security, storage, databases, auth, console, infrastructure
---

Appwrite 2.6 is now available for self-hosting.

This release includes:

- Remove location, device, and capture-time metadata from new image uploads using the bucket's **Image metadata** setting. Color profiles and orientation are preserved; stripping is off by default, applies within the read-buffer size limit, and is unavailable through the S3-compatible API (#14351).
- Use resource descriptions through the API for databases, tables/collections, columns/attributes, indexes, buckets, functions, sites, variables, topics, and keys (#14471, #14595). This is an API addition; the pinned Console does not provide editors for every description field.
- Configure periodic password changes from the Console's Auth policies page, and use custom password deny lists through the project policy API (#14602, #14499).
- Refresh outbound TLS trust to reject the compromised eMudhra certificate chains; both the runtime base and independent Composer stage carry the fix (#14719).
- Upgrade to self-hosted Console 1.2.97, including the bucket metadata setting, password-rotation policy card, time-of-day selection in date ranges, and one-minute chart intervals for short windows.

Back up your instance and follow the [upgrade instructions](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production/updates#upgrading-to-latest). Run the migration after upgrading from 2.5.0: this release adds schema fields.

